# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commercial routing (Phase 6)
#
# The public site asks the database ONE question — "who should receive this
# inquiry?" — through public.resolve_commercial_contact(country, language).
# These two values say where to ask it. Both are inlined into the static bundle
# at build time, which is why only the ANON key belongs here: it grants EXECUTE
# on that one function and nothing else. The service-role key must never appear
# in this file, in this repository, or in a build of this site.
#
# Leave them unset and the site still works: every inquiry takes the global
# fallback path below, which is the correct behaviour for a preview build with
# no database behind it.
#
# ─── Phase 7 uses the same two values, and no others ─────────────────────────
# Lead capture added no environment variable. The two write endpoints are
# derived from the URL above:
#
#   create_public_lead(...)                 records a project inquiry
#   record_public_lead_channel_click(...)   records that a channel was pressed
#
# Both are SECURITY DEFINER functions that return { success }. The anon key
# still holds NO table grant on any lead or commercial table — the complete set
# of things it can do is call those two plus the resolver. See
# docs/lead-capture.md §6.
#
# With them unset, the contact channels still work and the inquiry form reports
# that it could not send, rather than silently discarding what somebody wrote.
#
# ─── Phase 9: which project this must point at ───────────────────────────────
# Unchained Business's own Supabase project, and no other.
#
# Until 2026-09-05 this pointed at jkjsjojwlrzpcpggqgws — TanCerca's project,
# where the Unchained schema lived as a set of extra tables. One project meant
# one auth.users, which meant an address registered by a TanCerca CUSTOMER was
# the same account when Unchained tried to invite a specialist. That is not a
# configuration detail; it is the reason "this email is already registered" was
# reported for somebody who had never touched Unchained.
#
# The rule, for this site and for every site this agency runs afterwards: one
# web property, one Supabase project. Not one project with a product column.
# If you find yourself pasting another site's project ref in here to save
# creating one, that is the mistake this file exists to prevent. See
# docs/database-isolation.md.
#
# The service-role key of ANY project still must never appear in this file, in
# this repository, or in a build of this site. The anon key below can call
# exactly three functions and read no table at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-unchained-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Global fallback contact (§22)
#
# Shown only when no regional representative can be determined — an unrouted
# country, a region with nobody active, or a resolver that could not be reached.
#
# Every one of these is OPTIONAL and every one is validated: a malformed value
# produces no button rather than a broken one. Nothing is defaulted to a
# plausible-looking address, because a contact nobody reads is worse than an
# honest "we could not determine a regional contact".
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_BOOKING_URL defaults to siteConfig.bookingUrl.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_WHATSAPP=+34600000000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_TELEGRAM=unchainedbusiness
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_EMAIL=hello@unchainedbusiness.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_BOOKING_URL=https://cal.com/unchained/intro
